 "claim": "THE ASYMPTOTIC ROUTE, measured. If M_t^(r) is a Hausdorff moment sequence then by Hausdorff's theorem every alternating difference is nonnegative, i.e. K_r >= 0 for EVERY depth at once. Measured at the shore, that holds in an explicit corner with TWO sharp boundaries: (1) a lam threshold with lam*/n staying BOUNDED (1.33 to 2.86 over n = 12..60, i.e. lam ~> 2n), and (2) a depth boundary that is exact: at lam = 10^4 the largest depth with the property is j = n/2 + 1 in every case tested (n = 12..44). So the route proves all depths up to n/2 + 1 in the region lam ~> 2n by a classical theorem, and does NOT reach the complementary region -- which is unbounded, so this is a corner, not a finish.",
